---
description: Verify the HTTP implementation against its generated OpenAPI document with apidrifter
globs: ["src/**", "openapi.json", "**/routes/**", "**/controllers/**", "**/handlers/**", "**/api/**"]
alwaysApply: false
---

When you add or change an HTTP endpoint or a Zod schema that feeds the OpenAPI document:

1. Start the service locally (`npm start`, port 3000). The spec is at
   http://localhost:3000/openapi.json.
2. `npx -y apidrifter plan http://localhost:3000/openapi.json --out plan.json`, then write a
   filled plan with realistic values for the slots the engine cannot infer.
3. `npx -y apidrifter run http://localhost:3000/openapi.json --base-url http://localhost:3000 --plan filled.json --format markdown`.
   http:// is only allowed for localhost. Never put real credentials in the plan or the
   command line; use `--bearer-env VAR`.
4. For each finding decide which side is the source of truth, fix that side, and rerun until
   the report is clean. Do not loosen the schema to silence findings.
5. Run `npm run spec` so the committed openapi.json matches, and paste the Markdown report
   into the pull request.
